## Port of pumpkin/src/net/java/play.rs
## PARTIAL: pumpkin/src/net/java/play.rs - every handler is here and routed; what each calls that is not ported stops at a hook and says so in place. No plugin events anywhere (`send_cancellable!` runs its `after`). `handle_chat_command`, `handle_command_suggestion` wait on src/command's dispatcher, held back by the compiler bug. `handle_attack` and the attack half of `handle_interact` reach `Player::attack`, which needs damage (living.rs). `handle_use_item` and `prepare_hand_item_for_use` need `item_registry`, status effects and cooldowns. `handle_set_command_block`, `handle_set_jigsaw_block`, `handle_jigsaw_generate` and `handle_sign_update` need block entities. `handle_place_recipe` needs a crafting grid recipe placement against `generated/recipes`, `handle_pick_item_from_entity` entities, `handle_select_trade` a merchant, `handle_move_vehicle` and `handle_paddle_boat` vehicles. `validate_chat_session` has no Mojang public keys to check against, since they come over the HTTP that is missing, and refuses.
##
## Upstream's movement handlers differ in one place that is kept: `handle_position` jumps when the client left the
## ground, `handle_position_rotation` when it did not. Both are as upstream wrote them.

